WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.148 --> 00:00:01.975
Good morning Believe Nation, it's Evan.

00:00:01.975 --> 00:00:04.655
My one word is believe,
and I believe in people

00:00:04.655 --> 00:00:06.350
more than they believe in themselves.

00:00:06.350 --> 00:00:09.021
And my sincere hope is
that if you see in yourself

00:00:09.021 --> 00:00:12.433
what I see in you, you'll be
able to change the planet.

00:00:12.433 --> 00:00:13.702
So to help you on your journey,

00:00:13.702 --> 00:00:16.236
today's message is "Use fear."

00:00:16.236 --> 00:00:18.145
Over to you, Tony Robbins.

00:00:18.145 --> 00:00:19.724
(rooster crows)

00:00:19.724 --> 00:00:20.737
(hip hop beat)

00:00:20.737 --> 00:00:22.762
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:22.762 --> 00:00:25.403
♫ Espresso keep me going

00:00:25.403 --> 00:00:29.574
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:29.574 --> 00:00:30.593
The only way to deal with fear

00:00:30.593 --> 00:00:32.802
that I've found in my
life, is a couple ways.

00:00:32.802 --> 00:00:35.964
One of those ways is to turn it on itself,

00:00:35.964 --> 00:00:38.380
and ask yourself, "What am I afraid of?

00:00:38.380 --> 00:00:39.280
"I'm afraid of that?

00:00:39.280 --> 00:00:41.962
"I got to be more afraid of
what I'm going to miss out on.

00:00:41.962 --> 00:00:43.036
"Missing out on my mission.

00:00:43.036 --> 00:00:45.223
"Missing out on who I'm supposed to be."

00:00:45.223 --> 00:00:46.355
In other words, if you're not going

00:00:46.355 --> 00:00:47.990
to get rid of fear, then use fear.

00:00:47.990 --> 00:00:49.360
Use fear, or it uses you.

00:00:49.360 --> 00:00:50.797
It's that simple.

00:00:50.797 --> 00:00:52.615
So you got to say, "Okay, what's the price

00:00:52.615 --> 00:00:53.975
"if I just stay doing this?

00:00:53.975 --> 00:00:56.681
"What's the price, I
need to really get scared

00:00:56.681 --> 00:00:59.239
"If I learn all this and
I don't follow through."

00:00:59.239 --> 00:01:01.273
That's something to be scared about.

00:01:01.273 --> 00:01:03.531
And then that fear will
get you over your fear.

00:01:03.531 --> 00:01:06.082
It'll push you through.
Turn fear on itself.

00:01:06.082 --> 00:01:08.314
Second way you can do it, is use what,

00:01:08.314 --> 00:01:09.606
you've probably heard me
say 'cause I've used it

00:01:09.606 --> 00:01:12.992
since I was 17, is my little
rocking chair test, right?

00:01:12.992 --> 00:01:15.122
I'm going to sit myself
in my rocking chair,

00:01:15.122 --> 00:01:17.940
I'm 85 years old and
looking back on my life,

00:01:17.940 --> 00:01:21.671
and I say, "I didn't do this, or I did."

00:01:21.671 --> 00:01:23.889
So I like to use fear
in two different ways.

00:01:23.889 --> 00:01:25.759
The first is the rocking chair test.

00:01:25.759 --> 00:01:28.513
It's, "Will I regret this
when I'm on my deathbed,

00:01:28.513 --> 00:01:31.472
"when I'm 80, 90, 100, 250 years old."

00:01:31.472 --> 00:01:33.655
However long we're living
at that point in the future.

00:01:33.655 --> 00:01:35.014
"Will I regret this?"

00:01:35.014 --> 00:01:37.277
And that was something that I learned

00:01:37.277 --> 00:01:40.232
when I was 18, 19 years old,

00:01:40.232 --> 00:01:41.693
and it's been one of the
most powerful lessons

00:01:41.693 --> 00:01:43.702
that has had an impact on me,

00:01:43.702 --> 00:01:45.398
that I had this moment in my life,

00:01:45.398 --> 00:01:47.233
I've talked about Paris and the girl story

00:01:47.233 --> 00:01:49.240
that I had before, and from there

00:01:49.240 --> 00:01:50.913
I decided that I don't
want to live with regret.

00:01:50.913 --> 00:01:53.633
Like, I can deal with short-term pain,

00:01:53.633 --> 00:01:55.519
but I can't deal with not knowing.

00:01:55.519 --> 00:01:57.989
And that led me to join
the start-up company,

00:01:57.989 --> 00:02:01.418
and ever since, if I've
come across a situation

00:02:01.418 --> 00:02:04.088
and I'm going to, feel like
I'm going to regret it,

00:02:04.088 --> 00:02:07.044
like I want to say yes
but I'm really afraid

00:02:07.044 --> 00:02:09.603
because of whatever short-term
impact there might be,

00:02:09.603 --> 00:02:11.855
I just make the longer-term fear

00:02:11.855 --> 00:02:14.185
bigger than the short-term fear.

00:02:14.185 --> 00:02:17.502
So I'm more afraid to miss out
on a lifetime of opportunity,

00:02:17.502 --> 00:02:21.065
versus the short-term fear
of it not working out.

00:02:21.065 --> 00:02:24.352
And if you can catch yourself
when you feel those moments

00:02:24.352 --> 00:02:27.324
of, "I'm just finding practical reasons

00:02:27.324 --> 00:02:30.997
"why I shouldn't do this,
but really it's just fear."

00:02:30.997 --> 00:02:32.841
I find that that really helps me

00:02:32.841 --> 00:02:34.318
thinking about the long-term,

00:02:34.318 --> 00:02:35.552
and whenever I have a major decision

00:02:35.552 --> 00:02:39.235
that I'm unsure about, I imagine my life

00:02:39.235 --> 00:02:41.044
on my deathbed, rocking chair test,

00:02:41.044 --> 00:02:42.881
looking back, "Am I going to regret this?"

00:02:42.881 --> 00:02:44.715
And if it's yes, if I'm going to regret

00:02:44.715 --> 00:02:47.402
not taking action, then I
know I have to take action

00:02:47.402 --> 00:02:49.243
however scary that may be short-term.

00:02:49.243 --> 00:02:51.155
The second thing that I use fear for

00:02:51.155 --> 00:02:54.144
is building the muscle, is
my muscle-building test.

00:02:54.144 --> 00:02:56.696
And that's where I want to get used to

00:02:56.696 --> 00:02:59.434
being uncomfortable, I want to get used to

00:02:59.434 --> 00:03:00.680
if I'm afraid of something,

00:03:00.680 --> 00:03:03.161
not just always shrinking down.

00:03:03.161 --> 00:03:05.192
And the hardest part,
I think for most people

00:03:05.192 --> 00:03:07.357
is to catch it, because
again we come up with

00:03:07.357 --> 00:03:09.948
these rational reasons why
we shouldn't do something,

00:03:09.948 --> 00:03:12.534
where really it's just
that fear speaking out,

00:03:12.534 --> 00:03:14.750
so understanding the
"why" behind the "why,"

00:03:14.750 --> 00:03:16.806
really really important.

00:03:16.806 --> 00:03:20.316
And the more you say yes to those things,

00:03:20.316 --> 00:03:22.059
the more you stretch your comfort zone,

00:03:22.059 --> 00:03:24.626
just for the fact that you
were afraid of doing it,

00:03:24.626 --> 00:03:25.999
the more that muscle is going to build.

00:03:25.999 --> 00:03:27.504
And I've shared a number
of different examples

00:03:27.504 --> 00:03:29.195
in different videos of me, you know,

00:03:29.195 --> 00:03:31.467
dancing on the street, and being afraid

00:03:31.467 --> 00:03:33.158
of what people would say about me,

00:03:33.158 --> 00:03:34.670
or me trying to do snowboard jumps,

00:03:34.670 --> 00:03:35.767
and being afraid of what people

00:03:35.767 --> 00:03:38.242
would say or look at me, or even here,

00:03:38.242 --> 00:03:41.296
walking, making a video,
this is not a green screen.

00:03:41.296 --> 00:03:43.439
Somebody commented before,
"What green screen are you on?"

00:03:43.439 --> 00:03:44.656
I'm not on a green screen.

00:03:44.656 --> 00:03:46.493
This is the actual business that I own,

00:03:46.493 --> 00:03:48.620
Toronto Dance Salsa,
that's an actual window.

00:03:48.620 --> 00:03:51.694
There's real people walking behind.

00:03:51.694 --> 00:03:53.835
And at the start that can
be intimidating, right?

00:03:53.835 --> 00:03:55.171
That people are walking behind.

00:03:55.171 --> 00:03:57.607
Sometimes people like, look
in and see what's happening.

00:03:57.607 --> 00:04:01.206
And I have to worry, like,
"Are they judging me?"

00:04:01.206 --> 00:04:02.574
But the fact that I'm afraid of that

00:04:02.574 --> 00:04:04.215
means that I have to go out and do it.

00:04:04.215 --> 00:04:06.534
Just to see it, just to
get rid of that fear.

00:04:06.534 --> 00:04:08.998
And then what that does is
it expands my comfort zone.

00:04:08.998 --> 00:04:11.338
So that the next time I
do it, it's not as scary.

00:04:11.338 --> 00:04:12.516
And the next time it's not as scary,

00:04:12.516 --> 00:04:14.387
and the next time you lose the fear.

00:04:14.387 --> 00:04:16.437
So I'm not afraid to come here now,

00:04:16.437 --> 00:04:18.661
and speak with people walking by.

00:04:18.661 --> 00:04:21.022
But if you constantly
allow fear to beat you

00:04:21.022 --> 00:04:23.478
then even the smallest things,

00:04:23.478 --> 00:04:25.278
you're going to shrink down from.

00:04:25.278 --> 00:04:26.904
And when you have
opportunities that can serve

00:04:26.904 --> 00:04:28.666
your higher purpose, that can make

00:04:28.666 --> 00:04:30.952
a great life for yourself,
you're not going to do them

00:04:30.952 --> 00:04:32.145
because you're too afraid.

00:04:32.145 --> 00:04:34.418
'Cause you just live in
this tiny, little bubble.

00:04:34.418 --> 00:04:35.566
So if you can continue to expand,

00:04:35.566 --> 00:04:36.883
like the great things happen at the edge

00:04:36.883 --> 00:04:38.451
of your comfort zone.

00:04:38.451 --> 00:04:40.833
So if you can continue to
expand your comfort zone,

00:04:40.833 --> 00:04:42.048
more and more and more great things

00:04:42.048 --> 00:04:43.795
are going to happen to you.

00:04:43.795 --> 00:04:45.296
And so just recognizing it, whenever

00:04:45.296 --> 00:04:48.920
you can catch that fear, it
can make a big difference.

00:04:48.920 --> 00:04:51.220
If you decide to say yes,
to step into the fear,

00:04:51.220 --> 00:04:54.334
to lean in on it, and just do
it even though you are afraid.

00:04:54.334 --> 00:04:56.268
So those two tests,
the rocking chair test,

00:04:56.268 --> 00:04:58.438
look forward, if you're going to regret it

00:04:58.438 --> 00:05:00.463
for the rest of your life
then you have to say yes,

00:05:00.463 --> 00:05:01.659
you have to have the certainty,

00:05:01.659 --> 00:05:03.644
you have to know, and
deal with the short-term,

00:05:03.644 --> 00:05:05.597
potential failure of it not working out,

00:05:05.597 --> 00:05:08.923
versus the long-term,
for the rest of your life

00:05:08.923 --> 00:05:11.534
feeling like you're living with regret.

00:05:11.534 --> 00:05:13.699
And two, just building the muscle.

00:05:13.699 --> 00:05:15.641
Recognizing that the great things happen

00:05:15.641 --> 00:05:16.907
at the edge of your comfort zone,

00:05:16.907 --> 00:05:18.919
and the more you practice
stretching your comfort zone,

00:05:18.919 --> 00:05:20.588
the more great things are
going to happen to you.

00:05:20.588 --> 00:05:21.539
So the question of the day today is,

00:05:21.539 --> 00:05:23.877
I'm curious, how do you use fear?

00:05:23.877 --> 00:05:26.163
How have you used fear to help you

00:05:26.163 --> 00:05:27.431
in your business, in your life?

00:05:27.431 --> 00:05:29.507
I'd love to hear an example
if you want to share it.

00:05:29.507 --> 00:05:31.162
Please put it down in the comments below.

00:05:31.162 --> 00:05:32.844
And also if you're
responding with a comment

00:05:32.844 --> 00:05:34.632
in the first couple of hours
of this video going live,

00:05:34.632 --> 00:05:37.465
you have a chance to win
one of our two daily prizes.

