00:06:02.110 --> 00:06:05.527
♫ Espresso keep me going

00:06:08.753 --> 00:06:10.998
- When you experience
moments of self-doubt,

00:06:10.998 --> 00:06:13.517
how do you approach getting
out of the dark place?

00:06:13.517 --> 00:06:15.770
- I grandiose my way out of fear.

00:06:15.770 --> 00:06:17.848
(audience laughs)

00:06:17.848 --> 00:06:20.765
- [Robert] If you can imagine that.

00:06:25.041 --> 00:06:27.513
- [Woman] It's a good way. It's charming.

00:06:27.513 --> 00:06:28.346
- You know, it's like literally,

00:06:28.346 --> 00:06:29.195
it's like, "Okay, I'm going to do

00:06:29.195 --> 00:06:32.937
"one of the greatest
car chases of all time.

00:06:32.937 --> 00:06:35.903
"And if I don't, I'm not as talented

00:06:35.903 --> 00:06:37.868
"as I thought I was."

00:06:37.868 --> 00:06:40.619
And I will realize there's
a ceiling to my talent,

00:06:40.619 --> 00:06:42.059
right now I don't think there is,

00:06:42.059 --> 00:06:43.893
(audience laughs)

00:06:43.893 --> 00:06:45.954
But if I don't do, but if it's not one

00:06:45.954 --> 00:06:47.094
of the greatest car chases of all time,

00:06:47.094 --> 00:06:49.253
then I've failed, and I, there
is a ceiling to my talent,

00:06:49.253 --> 00:06:50.876
I'm not as good as I thought I was."

00:06:50.876 --> 00:06:52.922
And I said that to everybody.

00:06:52.922 --> 00:06:54.639
And was I scared?

00:06:54.639 --> 00:06:55.743
Yeah.

00:06:55.743 --> 00:06:58.391
I had trepidation going all the way,

00:06:58.391 --> 00:07:00.191
because it's mine to fail.

00:07:00.191 --> 00:07:03.680
And it's failing in
front of the mirror, too.

00:07:03.680 --> 00:07:05.075
Because I'll know if I did it or not,

00:07:05.075 --> 00:07:06.304
and I'll be like, "Okay."

00:07:06.304 --> 00:07:08.538
"You are not as good as
you thought you were."

00:07:08.538 --> 00:07:11.308
And that got me to Mt. Everest.

00:07:11.308 --> 00:07:12.612
- It's true, I remember
at one point he goes,

00:07:12.612 --> 00:07:14.438
"Robert, can you imagine you and me doing

00:07:14.438 --> 00:07:16.447
"this car chase together,
how great it's going to be?"

00:07:16.447 --> 00:07:18.160
And I'm like, "Hey man,
you're on your own brother."

00:07:18.160 --> 00:07:20.540
(audience laughs)

00:07:20.540 --> 00:07:23.742
"I ain't going out there, I got five kids.

00:07:23.742 --> 00:07:26.837
"I'm not doing 100 mile an hour bull.

00:07:26.837 --> 00:07:29.333
"You want to live the Vanishing
Point dream buddy, live it."

00:07:29.333 --> 00:07:32.126
(Quentin and Robert laugh)

00:07:32.126 --> 00:07:33.077
And he did it all by himself,

00:07:33.077 --> 00:07:34.580
and I'm so proud of him.

00:07:34.580 --> 00:07:36.280
- There's a scene in there
where you talked about

00:07:36.280 --> 00:07:39.280
um, bullies, and running from danger

00:07:40.841 --> 00:07:42.750
and things like that when you
were trying to help this kid.

00:07:42.750 --> 00:07:45.010
- Yeah, what happens is
this boy is being harassed

00:07:45.010 --> 00:07:46.775
by the neighborhood bully.

00:07:46.775 --> 00:07:48.432
And his father is encouraging his son

00:07:48.432 --> 00:07:50.610
to beat up this little boy.

00:07:50.610 --> 00:07:52.137
And I wrote this scene.

00:07:52.137 --> 00:07:54.224
I wrote this particular
scene in the script.

00:07:54.224 --> 00:07:55.166
And I was trying to think,

00:07:55.166 --> 00:07:58.244
"What can I write to encourage this boy

00:07:58.244 --> 00:07:59.743
"to handle the situation, you know,

00:07:59.743 --> 00:08:02.276
"with this bully in the neighborhood."

00:08:02.276 --> 00:08:04.127
And I'm spending days
trying to figure out,

00:08:04.127 --> 00:08:06.280
"What can I say to a boy?"

00:08:06.280 --> 00:08:08.536
And finally I came up with the answer,

00:08:08.536 --> 00:08:10.873
and it was a situation that I, as a child,

00:08:10.873 --> 00:08:12.555
had encountered about his age.

00:08:12.555 --> 00:08:14.583
I went to a school in Arizona

00:08:14.583 --> 00:08:17.547
that was mostly Indians
from the reservation.

00:08:17.547 --> 00:08:18.956
And there was this one Indian kid

00:08:18.956 --> 00:08:20.303
who just didn't like me, and every day

00:08:20.303 --> 00:08:22.389
he would chase me home from school.

00:08:22.389 --> 00:08:26.230
And uh, and I'd have to
run by this gas station

00:08:26.230 --> 00:08:27.988
and this mechanic would
watch me being chased

00:08:27.988 --> 00:08:30.521
by this Indian kid every day.

00:08:30.521 --> 00:08:32.397
And finally he just
couldn't handle it anymore.

00:08:32.397 --> 00:08:35.477
And he stopped me, and
made me face this boy.

00:08:35.477 --> 00:08:39.240
And I told him, I told him I was scared

00:08:39.240 --> 00:08:41.736
and he said, well, and what he said to me

00:08:41.736 --> 00:08:44.355
which is still true, which I remember,

00:08:44.355 --> 00:08:46.659
is that he says, "You know,
that running from your fear

00:08:46.659 --> 00:08:48.818
"is more painful than facing it."

00:08:48.818 --> 00:08:50.463
And that's something
I've always remembered.

00:08:50.463 --> 00:08:52.205
And this is what I relate to this boy,

00:08:52.205 --> 00:08:54.050
and of course eventually he has to face

00:08:54.050 --> 00:08:55.744
this fear in the film.
(audience applauds)

00:08:55.744 --> 00:08:57.957
- Be right back with more Chuck Norris.

00:08:57.957 --> 00:08:59.147
- [Interviewer] I see you in your basement

00:08:59.147 --> 00:09:02.446
like Batman with all machines and stuff.

00:09:02.446 --> 00:09:06.216
It's really precise I guess,
and really what you put,

00:09:06.216 --> 00:09:08.552
you know what you put
and then you go live.

00:09:08.552 --> 00:09:10.423
What's the difference? The risk?

00:09:10.423 --> 00:09:13.256
- The risk. You know, and the risk

00:09:14.818 --> 00:09:16.647
and I have stage fright, you know,

00:09:16.647 --> 00:09:19.359
and I never confronted the risk.

00:09:19.359 --> 00:09:20.651
Or when I did confront, I mean

00:09:20.651 --> 00:09:23.540
Belgium, 2000. The year 2000.

00:09:23.540 --> 00:09:26.819
That was, you have no
idea what it took them

00:09:26.819 --> 00:09:28.918
to get me to do it.

00:09:28.918 --> 00:09:30.241
- [Interviewer] And why did you say yes?

00:09:30.241 --> 00:09:31.374
- No no no no, I had a thousand,

00:09:31.374 --> 00:09:33.257
I had a thousand excuses why not to do it,

00:09:33.257 --> 00:09:36.174
and finally I did it, and it was...

00:09:39.460 --> 00:09:40.934
(sighs)

00:09:40.934 --> 00:09:44.341
Exquisitely horrifying, that's
the only way I can put it.

00:09:44.341 --> 00:09:45.240
- [Interviewer] Complex.

00:09:45.240 --> 00:09:49.063
- Yes. It was very, very, very complex.

00:09:49.063 --> 00:09:51.783
And what was really good

00:09:51.783 --> 00:09:55.604
was right at the beginning,
within like two seconds,

00:09:55.604 --> 00:09:59.226
I played just the worst wrong note

00:09:59.226 --> 00:10:03.393
and I could either stop and
cry, or I could laugh, right?

00:10:04.341 --> 00:10:05.480
And it didn't kill me.

00:10:05.480 --> 00:10:08.201
And nobody else out there,
nobody was throwing anything.

00:10:08.201 --> 00:10:10.342
You know? It was fine.

00:10:10.342 --> 00:10:14.877
Thank you to the people of
Ghent for not killing me.

00:10:14.877 --> 00:10:19.122
And giving me the courage,
you know, and the absurdity.

00:10:19.122 --> 00:10:21.825
You know, you have to be
able to laugh at yourself.

00:10:21.825 --> 00:10:25.356
And you have to learn
how to laugh at yourself.

